DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     cchheecckk--lliibb--ddeeppeennddss scans a port or package for shared libraries, and ver‐
     ify that all of them are properly recorded.

     cchheecckk--lliibb--ddeeppeennddss can either scan files from a built port after the _f_a_k_e
     _s_t_a_g_e from the WRKINST directory, or look directly inside a _p_a_c_k_a_g_e.

     Likewise, it can also verify dependencies of installed packages, or fig‐
     ure them out directly from the port directory.

     cchheecckk--lliibb--ddeeppeennddss actually consists of two distinct stages:

     ••   scan all binaries inside a package to extract libraries and rpaths,
         using objdump(1).

     ••   compare those libraries against the port's registered dependencies
         and report problems.

     The options are as follows:

     --BB _d_e_s_t_d_i_r
              Scan files under _d_e_s_t_d_i_r.

     --dd _p_k_g_r_e_p_o
              Look for all needed packages under directory _p_k_g_r_e_p_o.

     --DD _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y
              Create debug log files under _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y that show in more details
              the run of objdump(1).

     --ff       Give full reports of every file that requires a missing library.

     --FF _m_i_s_s_i_n_g
              Works in tandem with --SS.  Allow backsubstituting even if the
              _m_i_s_s_i_n_g library is actually not part of the actual WANTLIB of
              the package.  Mostly used to waive the presence of _p_t_h_r_e_a_d, a
              mandatory dependency of C++ libraries on some architectures.

     --ii       Read packing-list from standard input.

     --mm       Always show progress-meter, even if not run from terminal.

     --OO _d_e_s_t  Save result of first stage in file _d_e_s_t.

     --qq       Be quiet, do not emit ‘Extra:’ wantlibs unless there's also an
              actual problem.

     --SS _v_a_r=_v_a_l_u_e
              Recognize list of libraries listed in a variable, and replace
              said list with variable value.  For instance, --SS
              _C_O_M_P_I_L_E_R___L_I_B_C_X_X=_s_t_d_c_+_+ will replace ‘stdc++’ with
              ‘${COMPILER_LIBCXX}’ in WANTLIB lists for compatibility with
              both clang and gcc.  Order matters.  The first --SS option will be
              handled first.

     --ss _s_r_c   Don't scan, directly read result of first stage from file _s_r_c.

     --xx       Don't show progress-meter, even if run from terminal.

     If no _p_a_c_k_a_g_e is given, and the --ii option is used, cchheecckk--lliibb--ddeeppeennddss will
     retrieve the packing-list from stdin, and scan the package according to
     other options.

